From 558ce2b827d8d6751528ab6a19b1d3bacfd9d89e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 00:54:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] store: move the temporary name aside before it is removed

ReplaceFileIn, WriteFileAtomicIn and CreateFileAtomicIn no longer look
at the temporary name and then unlink it. written.dropTemp renames it
first to a new name of its own (.tmp- and 16 random hex digits, through
the root), looks at that name with Root.Lstat and os.SameFile, and
unlinks it only if it is the file written. An entry that another
process put under the temporary name is at most renamed, never removed,
and the error (ErrReplacedMeanwhile) names both names (review of task
34 A, hint of the second reviewer). The window between the Root.Lstat
and the unlink stays, now on a name that exists only from the rename on
and that no other process can know before; the comment of dropTemp
describes it, and the rename over an entry put under the new name
before it (64 random bits to guess). The directory is opened for the
unlink before the Root.Lstat (openDirIn, removeNameInDir on Linux and
AIX), so that the window holds no open any more.

The unlink that finds the new name gone (ENOENT) or a directory
(EISDIR) is ErrReplacedMeanwhile, after the link of CreateFileAtomicIn
and on the error paths alike, where removeTemp swallowed it before
(review of task 34 A, N1 of the second reviewer). When the check after
the link fails and the temporary name is foreign as well, the error of
CreateFileAtomicIn names both.

Tests: the error path of writeTempIn with a swapped temporary name and
a write that fails (EFBIG under RLIMIT_FSIZE 0, at the new hook point
"opened"); FD_CLOEXEC of the duplicate held; the ENOENT and EISDIR
branches at the new hook point "unlink" (reviews of task 34 A, N1 and
N2 of the first reviewer and its hints). The comment "a directory
never" is limited to Linux and AIX. The tests of publish expect the new
messages; publish itself is unchanged but for two comments.

Task: docs/tasks/36-nach-m1-nacht4b.md (Paket 36A)
